{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0166yFHypCWvCZgg6ovAtTv3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now I have comprehensive data. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary of Help/Version Flag Handling Patterns in go-unix-utils\n\nBased on analyzing multiple cmd/*/main.go files, here are the consistent patterns used across the repository:\n\n### 1. **Help Text Format**\n\nHelp text is consistently defined as a module-level const string:\n\n```go\nconst helpText = `Usage: ls [OPTION]... [FILE]...\nList information about the FILEs (the current directory by default).\nSort entries alphabetically if no flags given.\n\n  -a             do not ignore entries starting with .\n  -A             do not list implied . and ..\n  [more options...]\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n```\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- Usage line: `Usage: <cmd> [OPTION]... [FILE]...` or similar\n- Description paragraph (1-3 lines)\n- Option listing with 2-space indent for short options, ~15-20 chars for description\n- Long options (--help, --version) listed separately at end\n- Each option typically indented with 2 spaces, descriptions aligned\n\n**Example from ls (lines 23-49):**\n```go\nconst helpText = `Usage: ls [OPTION]... [FILE]...\nList information about the FILEs (the current directory by default).\nSort entries alphabetically if no flags given.\n\n  -a             do not ignore entries starting with .\n  -A             do not list implied . and ..\n  ...\n      --color[=WHEN]  colorize the output; WHEN can be 'always'\n                         (default if omitted), 'auto', or 'never'\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n`\n```\n\n**Example from sha256sum (lines 18-35):**\n```go\nconst helpText = `Usage: sha256sum [OPTION]... [FILE]...\nPrint or check SHA256 (256-bit) checksums.\n\nWith no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.\n  -b, --binary         read in binary mode\n  -c, --check          read checksums from the FILEs and check them\n      --tag            create a BSD-style checksum\n  -t, --text           read in text mode (default)\n  -z, --zero           end each output line with NUL, not newline,\n                         and disable file name escaping\n\nThe following five options are useful only when verifying checksums:\n      --quiet          don't print OK for each successfully verified file\n      --status         don't output anything, status code shows success\n  -w, --warn           warn about improperly formatted checksum lines\n      --help           display this help and exit\n      --version        output version information and exit\n`\n```\n\n### 2. **Version Text Format**\n\nVersion text is consistently defined as a module-level const string:\n\n```go\nconst versionText = `sha256sum (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n```\n\n**Format pattern:**\n```\n<command> (go-unix-utils) dev\n```\n\n**Examples from multiple files:**\n- ls: `ls (go-unix-utils) dev\\n`\n- sort: `sort (go-unix-utils) dev\\n`\n- sha256sum: `sha256sum (go-unix-utils) dev\\n`\n- head: `head (go-unix-utils) dev\\n`\n- uname: `uname (go-unix-utils) dev\\n`\n\n### 3. **How Flags Are Triggered**\n\nThe repository uses **direct `os.Exit(0)` calls immediately after printing**, never sentinel errors:\n\n**From ls/main.go (lines 104-109):**\n```go\ncase arg == \"--help\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n    os.Exit(0)\ncase arg == \"--version\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n    os.Exit(0)\n```\n\n**From sort/main.go (lines 197-202):**\n```go\ncase \"--help\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n    os.Exit(0)\ncase \"--version\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n    os.Exit(0)\n```\n\n**From sha256sum/main.go (lines 125-132):**\n```go\ncase \"--help\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n    os.Exit(0)\n    return true, 1\ncase \"--version\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n    os.Exit(0)\n    return true, 1\n```\n\n**From head/main.go (lines 147-149):**\n```go\ncase flag == \"--help\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n    os.Exit(0)\n```\n\n**From uname/main.go (lines 93-98):**\n```go\ncase a == \"--help\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n    os.Exit(0)\ncase a == \"--version\":\n    fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n    os.Exit(0)\n```\n\n### 4. **Additional Error Handling Patterns**\n\nWhen flags are invalid, the code typically follows:\n\n```go\n// Error on invalid option\nfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ls: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", ch)\nfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'ls --help' for more information.\")\nos.Exit(2)\n```\n\nOr for parsing errors:\n```go\nfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sort: %s\\n\", err)\nfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Try 'sort --help' for more information.\\n\")\nos.Exit(2)\n```\n\n### 5. **Key File Locations**\n\nAll these patterns are found in:\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5531/cmd/ls/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5531/cmd/sort/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5531/cmd/sha256sum/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5531/cmd/head/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5531/cmd/tail/main.go`\n- `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5531/cmd/uname/main.go`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68deebab-f5bb-427b-a51f-3987a7551d02","uuid":"fed48963-f560-4f0d-b1cf-5523145394ae","timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:49:35.133Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5531, find how other cmd/ utilities handle --help and --version flags. Look at a few different